<title>USA: N.Y. business loans fell $148 mln in April 23 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans fell $148 mln in April 23 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $148 million to $45,865 million in the week ended April 23, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $153 million to $46,124 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $7,942 million to $853,606 million.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
